    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d493">

                <pb facs="0635" n="523" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg523"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123J634/355: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-26T17:00:00+08:00">June 26, 1935—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 26—10:07 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>317. Department’s 181, June 21, 6 p.m. I appreciate this evidence of the
                    President’s continued confidence. The information contained in the Department’s
                    telegram was conveyed orally to the Foreign Office by Lockhart<anchor n="17"
                        xml:id="d493-f1"/> on the 25th and Lockhart was informed that President Lin
                        Sen<anchor n="18" xml:id="d493-f2"/> who is ill has gone to Kuling for the
                    summer and will not return to Nanking until September. Before he left he fixed
                    September 14 as the date on which Doctor Trautmann, the newly appointed German
                    Ambassador, would present his letter of credence, the presentation to take place
                    at Nanking. The Foreign Office stated that it would be necessary to fix a date
                    subsequent to September 14th for me to present my letters of credence at
                    Nanking. I am instructing Nanking to hold letter of credence until appointed
                        time.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d493-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d493-f1" n="17" xml:id="d493-f1-content">
                <p>Frank P. Lockhart, Counselor of Legation in China.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d493-f2" n="18" xml:id="d493-f2-content">
                <p>President of the Chinese National Government.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d493-f3" n="19" xml:id="d493-f3-content">
                <p>The Minister in China informed the Department, in his telegram No. 347, July 10,
                    2 p.m., that President Lin Sen had designated September 17 as the date on which
                    he would accept the Minister’s letter of credence (123J634/357).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
